---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";

const lockups = [
  {
    title: "Primary Color",
    detail: "Multicolor mark with a Core Graphite wordmark for light surfaces.",
    src: "/brand/lockups/primary-color.svg",
    alt: "VINASIG multicolor logo with a Core Graphite wordmark",
    variant: "light",
    file: "primary-color.svg",
  },
  {
    title: "Color Black",
    detail: "Multicolor mark with a black wordmark for light surfaces.",
    src: "/brand/lockups/color-black.svg",
    alt: "VINASIG multicolor logo with a black wordmark",
    variant: "light",
    file: "color-black.svg",
  },
  {
    title: "Reversed",
    detail: "Multicolor mark with a white wordmark for dark surfaces.",
    src: "/brand/lockups/reversed.svg",
    alt: "VINASIG multicolor logo with a white wordmark",
    variant: "dark",
    file: "reversed.svg",
  },
  {
    title: "Monochrome Black",
    detail: "Single-color black lockup for light surfaces.",
    src: "/brand/lockups/monochrome-black.svg",
    alt: "VINASIG black monochrome logo",
    variant: "light",
    file: "monochrome-black.svg",
  },
  {
    title: "Monochrome White",
    detail: "Single-color white lockup for dark surfaces.",
    src: "/brand/lockups/monochrome-white.svg",
    alt: "VINASIG white monochrome logo",
    variant: "dark",
    file: "monochrome-white.svg",
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Brand & logo"
  description="Choose from the existing VINASIG logo exports and see where each variant fits."
  eyebrow="Identity guidance in draft"
>
  <section class="rule-callout" aria-label="Guidance status">
    <Icon name="info" class="callout-icon" />
    <div>
      <strong>Usage recommendations are a draft</strong>
      <p>Variant names and master sizes come from the supplied asset package. Recommendations on this page need owner review before they become organization-wide rules.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="concept-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">The identity</p><h2 id="concept-title">Four agents, one shared objective</h2></div>
      <p>The pixel-art mark places four agents around a shared negative-space core.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="identity-grid">
      <article class="card identity-card">
        <div class="logo-preview logo-preview--mark">
          <img src="/brand/marks/primary-mark.svg" alt="VINASIG four-agent Primary Brand Mark" width="25" height="25" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Primary Brand Mark master at 25 × 25 px</p>
          <p class="card-copy">Scout observes. Thinker reasons. Builder acts. Auditor evaluates. The symbol represents a coordinated, iterative workflow.</p>
          <div class="download-actions">
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/brand/marks/primary-mark.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/brand/marks/primary-mark-1000.png" download>1000 × 1000 PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card identity-card">
        <div class="logo-preview logo-preview--contained">
          <img src="/brand/marks/contained-mark.svg" alt="VINASIG Contained Brand Mark on its white square canvas" width="27" height="27" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Contained Brand Mark master at 27 × 27 px</p>
          <p class="card-copy">The supplied contained export has a white square canvas. Its larger PNG export is available for square profile and avatar placements.</p>
          <div class="download-actions">
            <a class="button button-secondary" href="/brand/marks/contained-mark.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
            <a class="text-link" href="/brand/marks/contained-mark-1080.png" download>1080 × 1080 PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="lockups-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Logo with wordmark</p><h2 id="lockups-title">Choose a horizontal lockup</h2></div>
      <p>Use a lockup when the VINASIG name should appear as part of the logo artwork. Each preview shows the supplied export on a suitable sample surface.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lockup-grid">
      {lockups.map((lockup) => (
        <article class="card lockup-card">
          <div class:list={["logo-preview", "logo-preview--lockup", lockup.variant === "dark" && "logo-preview--dark"]}>
            <img src={lockup.src} alt={lockup.alt} />
          </div>
          <div class="lockup-meta">
            <div><h3>{lockup.title}</h3><p class="card-copy">{lockup.detail}</p></div>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={lockup.src} download={lockup.file}>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="small-uses-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Compact contexts</p><h2 id="small-uses-title">Use the supplied small-format exports</h2></div>
      <p>Use the dedicated favicon files when a browser or platform asks for those icon dimensions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="two-column-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Favicon</h3>
        <div class="logo-preview logo-preview--favicons" aria-label="Favicon exports shown at increasing display sizes">
          <img src="/brand/favicons/favicon-16.png" alt="16 by 16 pixel VINASIG favicon" width="16" height="16" />
          <img src="/brand/favicons/favicon-32.png" alt="32 by 32 pixel VINASIG favicon" width="32" height="32" />
          <img src="/brand/favicons/favicon-48.png" alt="48 by 48 pixel VINASIG favicon" width="48" height="48" />
        </div>
        <p class="card-copy">Original supplied PNG sizes: 16 × 16, 32 × 32, and 48 × 48 pixels.</p>
        <div class="download-row">
          <a class="text-link" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-16.png" download>16 × 16 PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-32.png" download>32 × 32 PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/brand/favicons/favicon-48.png" download>48 × 48 PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h3>Monochrome Brand Mark</h3>
        <div class="mono-preview-grid">
          <div class="logo-preview logo-preview--mark"><img src="/brand/marks/monochrome-black.png" alt="Black monochrome VINASIG Brand Mark" /></div>
          <div class="logo-preview logo-preview--mark logo-preview--dark"><img src="/brand/marks/monochrome-white.png" alt="White monochrome VINASIG Brand Mark" /></div>
        </div>
        <p class="card-copy">Symbol-only exports for one-color contexts. Match black with a light surface and white with a dark surface.</p>
        <div class="download-row">
          <a class="text-link" href="/brand/marks/monochrome-black.png" download>Black PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/brand/marks/monochrome-white.png" download>White PNG&nbsp;<Icon name="externalLink" class="text-link-icon" /></a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="usage-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">For people and agents</p><h2 id="usage-title">Use the artwork as supplied</h2></div>
      <p>These are practical draft recommendations, not approved policy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="two-column-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Recommended</h3>
        <ul class="usage-list">
          <li>Choose the official variant that fits the background and the space available.</li>
          <li>Use the supplied SVG for scalable contexts or the closest matching PNG size.</li>
          <li>Keep the complete mark or lockup visible and preserve its proportions.</li>
          <li>Check the result at the size where people will actually see it.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Avoid</h3>
        <ul class="usage-list">
          <li>Do not crop, stretch, recolor, add effects, or redraw the logo.</li>
          <li>Do not replace or re-typeset the wordmark inside a lockup.</li>
          <li>Do not enlarge a small raster export when a larger supplied file is available.</li>
          <li>Do not invent a minimum size or clear-space measurement. Neither is specified in the source package.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="source-title">
    <div class="rule-callout">
      <Icon name="info" class="callout-icon" />
      <div>
        <strong>Source and rights</strong>
        <p>These files are exact copies of selected exports in the VINASIG Brand Assets archive. This repository does not add a license for the logo artwork. The supplied materials do not record a verified author name, so this guide does not assign one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note" id="source-title">The source archive contains <code>VINASIG_Logo_Story.md</code> and <code>99_Evidence/CREATION_RECORD.md</code>. Edit the original artwork there. These copies are website-ready exports.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
